  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "What is the value of \\[\\dfrac{2^{2014} + 2^{2012}}{2^{2014} - 2^{2012}}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-1\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(2013\\)",
    "E": "\\(2^{4024}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The exponents differ by only \\(2\\), so dividing by \\(2^{2012}\\) turns the large powers into small numbers. Since \\(2^{2014}=4\\cdot2^{2012}\\), the original denominator is \\(3\\cdot2^{2012}>0\\).\n\nDividing numerator and denominator by the nonzero number \\(2^{2012}\\) gives\n\\[\n\\frac{2^{2014}+2^{2012}}{2^{2014}-2^{2012}}\n=\\frac{2^{2014-2012}+1}{2^{2014-2012}-1}\n=\\frac{4+1}{4-1}\n=\\frac53.\n\\]\nThe value is \\(\\frac53\\), choice C.",
